    "intro_html":  "Chapli kebab is the flat, spiced patty of northwest Pakistan, cumin and coriander forward with tomato and green chili worked right into the meat. Traditionally they hit a hot pan of oil. We put them on sheet pans and finish under the broiler, which means you can make fourteen servings without standing over a skillet all afternoon. Over rice they come to \u003cstrong\u003e571 calories and 34 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.83\u003c/strong\u003e.",
